  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14198769/assets/00a9225cc13ee00a921618d630a1fffc071852d9dfbe4dcd16efbfba50ebc8a0.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for a sample of paired observations is shown above. What vectors correspond to the direction of the first principal component of the data?",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the *first principal component* of the data corresponds to the direction in which the data varies the most (the direction where we have the maximum variance).\n\nIn our diagram, the direction where the variance changes the most corresponds (approximately) to the vectors $a$ and $b,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14198769/assets/d84c44e48462718bb3bce6c49eb9b074ac0b529543594fd0861e7f4d96ce6996.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$a$  and $b$ only.\"",
